WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:08.508
In this video, we'll turn
tonight's feedback into my-taste,

2
00:00:08.508 --> 00:00:11.572
a skill every prototype follows from now on.

3
00:00:11.572 --> 00:00:14.566
This is a real run, with the waits sped up.

4
00:00:15.878 --> 00:00:19.057
It reads tonight's sessions
on this laptop: the

5
00:00:19.057 --> 00:00:22.505
steers we sent, and the
toolbar we picked, and why.

6
00:00:24.085 --> 00:00:29.154
Five rules, each with where it came from.
Nothing is saved until you say so.

7
00:00:31.506 --> 00:00:33.563
This demo has no marked-up screenshot,

8
00:00:33.563 --> 00:00:36.431
so it says it couldn't find
one, instead of guessing.

9
00:00:38.824 --> 00:00:42.295
The rest match tonight's
steers: bigger targets,

10
00:00:42.295 --> 00:00:45.406
labels when there's room, one accent color.

11
00:00:45.406 --> 00:00:46.418
Save all five.

12
00:00:49.587 --> 00:00:51.806
Saved, and the skill check passed.

13
00:00:51.806 --> 00:00:54.809
An update log keeps where each rule came from,

14
00:00:54.809 --> 00:00:57.354
even why we picked the labeled toolbar.

15
00:01:01.141 --> 00:01:04.651
From now on, when you ask for a
prototype, my-taste comes along.

16
00:01:04.651 --> 00:01:07.558
Next, we'll keep it current
with a weekly automation.
